Do not include hosts:, vars:, or any playbook-level headers. Only output valid task entries or blocks as expected in a role.  

Task 1: Import assert.yml
Description Task 1: Import the assert.yml file to perform initial validations and checks on the localhost.

Task 2: Install required software
Description Task 2: Install software packages listed in the users_requirements variable if it is not empty.

Task 3: Loop over users_groups
Description Task 3: Include the group.yml file for each group in the users_groups variable to manage groups if the variable is defined.

Task 4: Ensure the /etc/sudoers.d directory is included
Description Task 4: Add an entry to /etc/sudoers to include the /etc/sudoers.d directory if the users_sudo_includedir variable is set.

Task 5: Loop over users
Description Task 5: Include the user.yml file for each user in the users variable to manage users if the variable is defined.

Task 6: Manage cron permission
Description Task 6: Template the cron.allow.j2 file to /etc/cron.allow if the users_cron_allow variable is set.

Task 7: Check existence of /etc/cron.allow
Description Task 7: Ensure /etc/cron.allow does not exist if the users_cron_allow variable is not set.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook:
---

- import_tasks: assert.yml

- name: Install required software
  package:
    name: "{{ users_requirements }}"
    state: present
  when: users_requirements is defined

- include_tasks: group.yml
  loop: "{{ users_groups }}"
  loop_control:
    loop_var: user_group
  when: users_groups is defined

- name: Ensure /etc/sudoers.d directory is included
  lineinfile:
    path: /etc/sudoers
    line: '#includedir /etc/sudoers.d'
    state: present
  when: users_sudo_includedir is defined

- include_tasks: user.yml
  loop: "{{ users }}"
  loop_control:
    loop_var: user
  when: users is defined

- name: Manage cron permission
  template:
    src: cron.allow.j2
    dest: /etc/cron.allow
  when: users_cron_allow is defined

- name: Check existence of /etc/cron.allow
  file:
    path: /etc/cron.allow
    state: absent
  when: users_cron_allow is not defined


